## 8. Side-effects and field mutations in the create flow (exhaustive)

Mutations to the incoming `OwnerFieldsDto` (in `addOwner`):
- `ownerFieldsDto.setEmail(...)` — inside `normalizeEmail` (lines 210 & 217): blank→`null`; otherwise trimmed + lower-cased. Returns false (→400) if a present email fails `EMAIL_PATTERN` (`^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9-]+(\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)+$`, line 65-66).
- `ownerFieldsDto.setAddress(canonicalAddress)` (line 132) — normalized by `normalizeAddress` (lines 227-244): trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations `ST→STREET, RD→ROAD, AVE→AVENUE` (`ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS`, lines 72-73). Blank after normalize →400.
- `ownerFieldsDto.setTelephone(normalizedTelephone)` (line 181) — E.164 via `toE164` (lines 270-291): strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps explicit `+CC`, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; must be 8-15 digits else →400.

Mutations to the new `Owner` entity before save:
- `owner.setRegistrationDate(registrationDate)` (line 184) — defaults to `LocalDate.now()` if absent (server date; note current date is 2026-08-10), then rolled forward off weekends by `toBusinessDay` (lines 348-354).
- `owner.setCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(city, lastName))` (line 188) — format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`; the `NNNN` sequence = `countOwnersInCity(city)+1` (lines 316-321), derived from a full `findAllOwners()` scan.
- `owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(firstName, lastName))` (line 191) — count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive), via `findAllOwners()` (lines 307-314).
- `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` (line 183) copies firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone/email/registrationDate; it explicitly ignores `id` and `pets` (mapper `@Mapping(target="id"/"pets", ignore=true)`, `OwnerMapper.java:109-111`; generated `OwnerMapperImpl.toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` lines 77-94). So a newly created owner has no pets; the `@OneToMany(cascade=ALL)` cascade save of pets is not exercised on create.

Reject/short-circuit validations (in order) with their HTTP statuses:
1. Invalid present email → 400 (line 123)
2. Blank normalized address → 400 (line 130)
3. City at capacity (`countOwnersInCity >= 50`) → 409 CONFLICT (line 136)
4. Telephone not E.164-convertible → 400 (line 141)
5. Telephone already in use (E.164-compared) → 409 CONFLICT (line 150)
6. Duplicate household (same normalized last name + address) unless `sharesHousehold==true` → 409 CONFLICT (line 163)
7. Daily sign-up limit (`countOwnersRegisteredOn(businessDay) >= 100`) → 429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS (line 179)

Persistence side-effect:
- `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (line 192) → `ownerRepository.save` → SQL `INSERT` into `owners`. DB-level constraints from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/h2/schema.sql` (lines 31-42): `first_name/last_name/address/city/telephone NOT NULL`; column widths `first_name VARCHAR(30)`, `last_name VARCHAR(30)`, `address VARCHAR(255)`, `city VARCHAR(80)`, `telephone VARCHAR(20)`, `email VARCHAR(255)`, `customer_code VARCHAR(20)`. There is no unique constraint on telephone or on last_name+address at the DB level — those uniqueness rules are enforced only in application code (checks #5/#6 above).

Response-shaping side-effects (read-only, no DB writes, computed in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`, and generated `OwnerMapperImpl.toOwnerDto` lines 25-52):
- `displayName` = `"lastName, firstName"` (line 28-29)
- `initials` (lines 72-75)
- `householdId` = first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 of `normalizedLastName|normalizedAddress` (lines 83-98)
- `membershipNumber` = `"<customerCode>-M<YY>"` from registrationDate year (lines 60-66)
- `membershipTier` = `SILVER` if `namesakeCount==0` and email present, else `BRONZE` (lines 50-54)
- `locality` from city→region table (Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD, else UNKNOWN) (lines 42-44)

Logging side-effects: only in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (SLF4J `logger.error/warn/debug`) on the error paths. No logging, no event publishing, no auditing, and no password encoding occur on the successful owner-create path.

Response on success: `201 CREATED` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header (lines 194-196).
